{"agent":"bg84","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The regression never builds the plan the bug describes. With F1–F3 already held and `cap=3`, `plan` takes the no-free-slot branch (`why` starts with the existing \"cap reached\" string). The failure mode in the task is the other branch: a free slot offered to a higher-ranked item that may have no lease, so the detail no longer says \"cap reached\" and a lane cannot tell wait from claim. Dropping `{named}` from only the `if slots:` assignment in `_plan.py` (the string that actually ships in that case) still satisfies both asserts. The test also never checks that a named claim of the capped id succeeds, so \"grants it now\" is an unpinned promise.","digest":"13c17c16b83bf9c5","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_reserved_slots.py:96","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_reserved_slots.py:96"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":2959,"diff_sha":"70f9361e0204fad13e35cb1731dec5c5d040758c8782ce3eedb3c6b87c018d97","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B30f9d383ba","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":38.1,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"d8b3d26e742060d7","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B30f9d383ba.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T175321Z-83d0ccf2.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794160401.1425545,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}],"review_id":"6c5f33f72d5e","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"55ffd953897e00df9be8efd540f4aec8c1c0f0db","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/core/schedule/_plan.py":"100644 071733a09d52a3fae27b6bcaff6251b309b0fdfa","tests/test_reserved_slots.py":"100644 e962d2f0e695105ad53c